---
layout: shell.webc
title: Components
description: Norn's WebC components for Eleventy, rendered from the packages themselves.
---
<h1>Components</h1>
<p class="lead">
	Norn is a set of un-opinionated WebC components and helpers for Eleventy. Every component in the three packages is rendered here by
	Eleventy from the packages themselves. Pick one for its examples, props, slots, and custom properties.
</p>
<template webc:for="category of $data.catalog.categories" webc:nokeep>
	<h2 @text="category.title"></h2>
	<p @text="category.description"></p>
	<norn-card-grid :@mono="true">
		<li webc:for="component of category.components">
			<norn-card>
				<h3><a :href="component.url" @text="component.name"></a></h3>
				<p @text="component.summaryText"></p>
			</norn-card>
		</li>
	</norn-card-grid>
</template>
<h2>Packages</h2>
<p>Each component ships in one of three packages.</p>
<ul>
	<li webc:for="pkg of $data.catalog.packages"><code @text="pkg.name"></code> <span @text="pkg.version"></span>: <span @text="pkg.description"></span></li>
</ul>
